# PicEdit - RAW Photo Editor

A lightweight, high-performance desktop RAW photo editor built with Python, PySide6 (Qt), OpenCV, and LibRaw (rawpy). Designed for modularity, clean architecture, and real-time interactive adjustments.

---

## Current Features

- **High-Performance RAW Pipeline:** Fast decoding of RAW files (Canon `.CR2`) using a dual-resolution approach (downscaled proxy buffer for real-time preview, native full-resolution for export).
- **LUT-Accelerated Tone Engine:** Sub-millisecond tonal processing using precomputed Look-Up Tables (`cv2.LUT`) throttled at ~60 FPS.
- **General Adjustments:**
  - Exposure Compensation ($\pm 2.0\text{ EV}$)
  - Contrast Adjustment
  - Highlights & Shadows Recovery
  - Whites & Blacks Point Anchoring
- **Interactive Tone Curves & Histogram:**
  - Master RGB and individual R, G, B channel spline manipulation.
  - Live real-time background luminance and color histogram.
  - Dynamic control point management (click to add, drag to adjust, double-click to reset).
- **Responsive Workspace Canvas:**
  - Smooth pan and zoom centered at cursor position.
  - Quick keyboard shortcuts:
    - `Space` (hold): Instant Before/After (Original vs. Edited) comparison.
    - `R`: Fit-to-screen view reset.
- **Collapsible Control Panels:** Expandable/collapsible accordion layout with per-section reset actions and double-click slider resets.
- **Export:** High-quality full-resolution JPEG export.

---

## Architecture & Design Patterns

The codebase follows **SOLID** principles and clean architecture practices:
- **Strategy Pattern (`ImageFilter`):** Decoupled image processing operations located in `src/filters/` (`general/` and `curves/`).
- **Single Responsibility (`RawLoader`, `ImageEngine`):** Strict boundary between raw sensor decoding, pipeline state management, and UI rendering.
- **Asynchronous & Throttled UI:** Decoupled input capture from frame rendering using timer debouncing.

